Participation in ensuring compliance of the company's activities with the current legislation. 

 Candidate wish list:  

Student of Law Faculty; 
Exceptional analytical skills; 
Ability to work in a team and communicate efficiently; 
Ability to adapt quickly; 
Clear writing and verbal ability. 

 We offer  
We offer working in fast growing business with professional management teams and value driven challenging and development oriented organizational culture. Here we have non-formal, creative and comfortable environment. If you enjoy diversity and fast pace then you are right person for this internship program and in this case there is the right environment provided for you to fulfil your potential.&nbsp; 
 APPLY:  
If you feel you have what it takes to be successful in this role, don't hesitate to apply. Since we will be interviewing candidates continuously send your application as soon as possible to be included in the recruitment process.

 BioMed Realty is seeking a Finance Graduate Intern to support the Asset Planning &amp; Analysis (AP&amp;A) team. This graduate internship provides hands-on experience in financial planning, forecasting, data analytics, and quality assurance within a fast-paced Finance function.  &nbsp;  
 You will work closely with the AP&amp;A team to support monthly and quarterly planning cycles and reporting processes. Through exposure to comprehensive financial models, real estate fundamentals, and forecast-input reviews, you will develop technical proficiency in financial analysis and business operations while contributing to key deliverables that support the organization’s planning and forecasting activities.  &nbsp;  
&nbsp; 
   Key Duties and Responsibilities    &nbsp;  
 The Finance Graduate Intern will support the AP&amp;A team under the guidance of experienced professionals, building skills while contributing to recurring planning, forecasting, and reporting activities.  &nbsp;  

  Financial Forecasting and Modeling Support:    Assist with cash flow model updates and leasing forecasts.  &nbsp;  


  Quarterly Planning and Reporting Review:    Support the AP&amp;A team during quarterly planning cycles by preparing and reviewing key materials, including meeting documentation, quarterly planning inputs, and internal reporting packages. Review materials for completeness, consistency, and accuracy.  &nbsp;  


  Lease-Up Analysis and Reporting:    Prepare summaries for internal planning and analysis purposes, supporting the team’s understanding of portfolio leasing activity and forecasting.  &nbsp;  


  Quality Assurance and Validation:    Review quarterly reporting materials to identify gaps, inconsistencies, or errors. Clearly flag issues and questions to help ensure deliverables are accurate and complete before finalization.  &nbsp;  


  Process Documentation and Learning:    Help advance and expand standard operating procedures (SOPs) and workflow documentation for AP&amp;A processes while learning best practices and contributing to team knowledge resources.  &nbsp;  

&nbsp; 
   Opportunities for Growth    &nbsp;  

